["② The NIIED president may impose disciplinary action on a GKS recipient in any of
the following cases;
1. Engagement in political activities or conduct that may bring the national
interests or the honor of the Republic of Korea into disrepute;
2. Committing harmful acts such as theft, assault, verbal abuse, and sexual assault
(including sexual harassment and misconduct);
3. Violation of any laws of the Republic of Korea or the recipient's home country.
4. Submission of false documents or providing incorrect information;
5. Breach of the pledge made to the NIIED;
6. Engaging in wrongful acts as a GKS recipient;
③ The NIIED president may take actions such as issuing a warning after a", 'resolution by the disciplinary committee in the following cases:
1. Offenses of a relatively trivial nature;
2. Extenuating circumstances, such as an unavoidable event;
Article 21 (Report of Criminal Prosecution, etc.) ① A GKS Recipient must immediately
report to the Institution if they are prosecuted in a criminal case. The NIIED
president may take disciplinary action against the recipient according to Article 20
if they fail to report.
② The president of the institution must immediately report any criminal charges
involving a GKS recipient to the NIIED president.
③ The NIIED president has the authority to suspend the scholarship of a GKS
recipient facing criminal charges.
④ The NIIED president may disqualify the scholarship according to Articles 19, and
10, or call for the Disciplinary Committee under Articles 20 to reach a decision.
⑤ The NIIED president may suspend scholarships and reclaim the benefits of
the GKS award. In such a case, the Disciplinary Committee will determine the', 'temporary departure length due to unavoidable circumstances;
4. Violation of the permitted scope of part-time employment as stipulated in Article
24, Paragraph 2;
5. A warning issued by the GKS Award Recipient Disciplinary Committee
(“Disciplinary Committee”) for other violations;
Article 19 (Disqualification) The NIIED president may disqualify the GKS recipient
based on the following grounds:
1. Expulsion from the Institution;
2. Failure to advance to the Institution after completing the Korean language
program as outlined in Article 5.
3. Failure to register within the Institution’s designated registration period;
4. Failure to re-enter the country without valid reasons after the Institution’s
specified semester start date;']
